# Backend standards

- All external HTTP goes through provider adapters with retry, backoff, and quota tracking
- Validate inputs/outputs with Zod (TS) or Pydantic (Python)
- Prefer idempotent upserts keyed by canonical or `(source, external_id)`
- Store raw provider payloads for replay when ingesting
- Never log API keys or full secrets
- Public write/ingest endpoints must be cron-protected or admin-only
- Use ORM parameterized queries only (Drizzle/Prisma/SQLAlchemy)
